From 07c4aafa03b5d9b11742cd250779ce8d62e1fef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:44:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] drm/msm/dp: Recompute eDP bpp once the link capabilities
 are known

msm_dp_display_set_mode() picks the output bpp with
msm_dp_panel_get_supported_bpp(), which keeps the highest depth whose
data rate fits in num_lanes * rate * 8. For eDP the sink capabilities
are only read in msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(), called from
msm_dp_display_prepare_link(), i.e. after mode_set. On the first enable
link_info is therefore still zero, nothing fits, and the panel is driven
at the 18 bpp minimum, which shows up as visible banding.

Seen on the ASUS Zenbook A14 (UX3407NA): 1920x1200@60 (154.26 MHz) on
HBR x2 has room for 24 bpp (3.70 of 4.32 Gbps), but dp_debug reports
bpp = 18 after boot and only a later modeset picks a deeper format.

Re-run the mode setup for eDP right after the plug handling has
populated link_info, before link training and stream setup consume the
bpp.

Signed-off-by: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index d48403f1d..b54318bbd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -638,9 +638,21 @@ static int msm_dp_display_prepare_link(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "sink_count=%d\n", dp->link->sink_count);
 
-	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp)
+	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp) {
+		struct drm_display_mode mode;
+
 		msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
 
+		/*
+		 * For eDP, mode_set runs before the sink's link capabilities
+		 * have been read, so the bpp was chosen against an empty
+		 * link_info and fell back to the 18 bpp minimum. Redo the
+		 * selection now that the link rate and lane count are known.
+		 */
+		drm_mode_copy(&mode, &dp->panel->msm_dp_mode.drm_mode);
+		msm_dp_display_set_mode(msm_dp_display, &mode, dp->panel);
+	}
+
 	rc = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&msm_dp_display->pdev->dev);
 	if (rc) {
 		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
-- 
